From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: The EE at its full rate while a movie plays (Full EE Speed in Movies)

Games that need a low EE Cycle Rate to keep their speed can stop their
movies with it: Guitar Hero's intro stops on its first frame at any rate
below 0 (-3, -6 and -8 tried, with and without cycle skipping), and plays at
0. A movie is what the IPU decodes; Counters' FMV detection (DoFMVSwitch,
once a vsync on the CPU thread) already knows when one starts and ends.

With FullEERateForMovies on (the default; Settings > Emulation, "Full EE
Speed in Movies", per game too) and a set rate below 0, the effective rate
is 0 while a movie plays and the set rate again a second after it ends. The
switch goes through EECycleRate::ApplyEffective like the governor's, which
patches the recompiler's charges in place; meanwhile the governor's own
moves are refused. Checked on an RG52 Mini: Guitar Hero at -8 plays its
intro to the title screen (full rate at 28 s, back to -8 at 64 s).

